  "revision": 4,
  "title": "Forked integration case runners never run the leak check",
  "description": "parallel_case_runner.h runs every case in a forked child that ends with _exit(), so LeakSanitizer never runs and ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1 sanitizer runs of the scheduler and other suites report no leaks whatever happens. With an explicit __lsan_do_recoverable_leak_check() after each scheduler case, the only remaining report is the framework escape buffer, FND-20261113004147-cf2e-indigo-xml-escape-buffer-finding-001. Next: after that is fixed, run the leak check in the case runner child before _exit() where LeakSanitizer is available.\n\nImported from .factory/findings/active/FND-20261113001457-32cc-scheduler-shutdown-command-leak-001.json (category: quality, blocking: no).",
